    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0179" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg137"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 70</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">850.33/12–1551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States High Commissioner for Germany
                        (</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">McCloy</hi><hi rendition="#italic">) to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d70-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonn</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-15T19:00:00+01:00">December 15,
                            1951—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>743. Adenauer suffered minor but sharp
                    rebuff at hand of Parliament Dec 13 when Council of Elders rejected his request
                    to schedule Schuman Plan debate before
                    Christmas.</p>
                <pb facs="0180" n="138" xml:id="pg138"/>
                <p>Difficulty arose when, at early session of Council of Elders, CSU Horlacher
                    allegedly slightly intoxicated broke coalition front by agreeing to SPD motion to postpone debate till Jan 3 taking
                    with him FDP and DP with CDU abstaining in resultant
                    confusion. Thereupon Adenauer summoned
                    coalition leaders reestablished majority front for debate Dec 18 and thereafter
                    attended second session of Council of Elders where he sharply demanded debate
                    before Christmas on ground he needed early ratification to strengthen hand in
                    coming international conferences. SPD deputies
                    cleverly avoiding issue of Schuman Plan
                    per se, roundly berated Chancellor for his highhanded treatment of Bundestag
                    citing numerous instances in which he had snubbed his own coalition floor
                    leaders. Smouldering resentment of latter was thus aroused and acrimonious
                    exchanges on issue of Adenauer attitude to
                    elected representatives ensued in which Adenauer found himself attacked by all sides. Finally Chancellor
                    apparently lost patience and told his attackers he didn’t care what they
                    decided. Council with somewhat sheepish concurrence of coalition representatives
                    then decided to hold debate Jan 9 when Parliament would normally reconvene
                    except for fact Chancellor will be unable to report ratification at Dec 27
                    meeting of EDC Ministers, no real damage has
                    been done save to his feelings and prestige. Incident may well have salutory
                    effect on tendency of Adenauer to ignore
                    Bundestag and ineptness of his subordinates notably Hallstein in dealing with Deputies. Furthermore by desisting
                    from rushing ratification thru Bundestag Chancellor may have deprived SPD of additional ammunition for attack on plan.
                    There is no reason to believe that ultimate ratification has been endangered. In
                    fact majority reported April at seventy odd may well run to nearer a hundred at
                    final vote.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCloy</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
